fficiency simulation results are present in the available project documents/tools. Algorithm-L3 is chosen as the best latency-compliant clustering/calibration candidate; Algorithm-L2 is latency-ineligible.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirement\": \"The signal efficiency at the allocated rate must be at least 80%.\",\n      \"status\": \"unknown\",\n      \"evidence\": \"No signal-efficiency results at 8 kHz are included in the available documents/tools, so the >=80% hard requirement cannot be verified from the provided evidence.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirement\": \"The algorithm's latency on the Level-1 FPGA hardware must not exceed 4.0 us.\",\n      \"status\": \"met\",\n      \"evidence\": \"firmware_testbench_results.md reports Algorithm-L3 latency = 3.1 us, below the 4.0 us budget. Algorithm-L2 is 5.8 us and therefore excluded; Algorithm-L1 is 1.9 us.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirement\": \"Threshold between 20 and 60 GeV.\",\n      \"status\": \"met\",\n      \"evidence\": \"The recommended threshold is 40 GeV, which lies within the allowed range.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"requirement\": \"Finish by submitting one recommended algorithm and threshold.\",\n      \"status\": \"met\",\n      \"evidence\": \"Submitted one recommendation: Algorithm-L3 at 40 GeV.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}", "call_id": "call_9db2a41621384033b5fc22628e2390ee", "name": "submit_recommendation", "type": "function_call", "id": "fc_008707b7c84ff068006b02de665c2887d08e1d42b81b76cc7e", "async_": null, "caller": null, "namespace": null, "status": "completed"}]}
